    3. place D dominoes one at a time; for each, pick random orientation (H/V), pick a random position, ensure all cells of the domino are black and the domino is 4-disconnected from all previously placed red pixels (Manhattan >= 2 from any existing red pixel)
    4. place S single red pixels one at a time; each must be 4-disconnected from all existing red pixels (Manhattan >= 2, i.e. no 4-adjacent red neighbor); Chebyshev >= 1 suffices
    5. verify at least 1 domino was placed
