17:     """
18:     Reconstruct each indicated pattern at matching isolated indicator pixels, mirroring red-indicated patterns first.
19: 
20:     Input structure:
21:     - The grid contains one or more multi-color patterns on a black background.
22:     - Each pattern contains a red or green indicator pixel.
23:     - Isolated red and green pixels elsewhere mark reconstruction targets.
24: 
25:     Rule:
26:     - Separate larger pattern sprites from isolated indicator pixels.
27:     - Mirror a pattern left-right when its embedded indicator is red.
28:     - Paste each pattern so its indicator aligns with every isolated pixel of the same color.
29: 
30:     Key insight:
31:     - The indicator color pairs each pattern with its destinations, and red additionally
32:       signals the mirror operation before stamping.
33:     """
34:     bg = Color.BLACK
35:     output_grid = input_grid.copy()
36: 
37:     objects = detect_objects(grid=input_grid, monochromatic=False, connectivity=8)
38:     pixels: list[np.ndarray] = []
39:     patterns: list[np.ndarray] = []
40: 
41:     for obj in objects:
42:         b = bbox(obj != bg)
43:         if b is None:
44:             continue
45:         spr = crop_bbox(obj, b)
46:         if spr.shape == (1, 1):
47:             pixels.append(obj)
48:         else:
49:             patterns.append(spr)
